---
description: Rules for data, types, Supabase, and external integrations
globs: data/**,types/**,lib/**,supabase/**
alwaysApply: false
---

# Data & Content

- Static content lives in `data/` as typed TypeScript exports.
- All shared types are in `types/` and re-exported from `types/index.ts`.
- Import types with `import type { X } from "@/types"`.

# Supabase

- Browser client: `lib/supabase/client.ts` (for client components).
- Server client: `lib/supabase/server.ts` (for server components/route handlers).
- Database types: `lib/supabase/types.ts` (will be auto-generated later).
- Schema changes: Add SQL migrations in `supabase/migrations/`.
- Never import Supabase in `components/` — data is passed via props from pages.

# Video Providers

- Provider logic is isolated in `lib/videos/providers.ts`.
- Supports: YouTube, Loom.
- Use `getEmbedUrl()` and `getThumbnailUrl()` — do not hardcode provider URLs elsewhere.
- To add a provider: add an entry to the `providers` record. No UI changes needed.

# Type Safety

- Keep types in sync with data structures.
- Prefer specific types over `any` or `unknown`.
- When adding a new data entity, create its type in `types/` first.
- Barrel-export from `types/index.ts`.

# Environment Variables

- Public (client-safe): `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- Server-only: no prefix (never access in client components)
- All variables documented in `.env.example`
